______________________________________________________________________________________
Exception:
CompletableFuture: In multi-threaded environment, 
exception thrown in a background thread may not be visible to the main thread/ propagate to main thread

Exceptions are wrapped in CompletionException, to handle them properly, we need to use following pipeline methods:
 1) exceptionally() --> act like catch block, used to logg the error and provide fallback values so the pipeline can continue
 2) handle()        --> act like finally block, it always executes, giving you access to both success(if any) and failure/exception(if any) cases
 3) whenComplete()  --> Used mainly to perform logging/cleanup operations, unlike handle, it doesn't allow you to modify the result
